      "prefLabel": "Merge steward",
      "title": "Merge steward",
      "notation": "merge-steward",
      "description": "Stewards writes to ONE watched ref -- a long-lived branch several processes write and something downstream consumes serially. The ref is a parameter of the LANE INSTANCE, not of this persona, so `main`, `gh-pages` and each `cat/cat-harness/*` store branch can each have a steward without a schema change; a ref qualifies when a declaring directory's `storage` (or `source`) names it, or it is `main`/`gh-pages`. On `main` that work is a merge train: composes it from the queue, attributes and ejects on red, lands at the tested SHA. On a route-keyed ref it is coalescing: batches the writes arriving in one window into a single write. Decides nothing the reprioritisation table or the owner has not -- placement is computed by merge-priority.dmn, and landing waits for the owner's release, given in the steward's own session as one card per batch. Records decisions on queue entries and windows, never the host's facts. Only the merge steward merges and re-pins, in every repository; the lane does not lapse, and a scheduled routine never merges (owner rulings, 2026-11-13). Its holding.neededWhen measures when the queue is contended (two or more active sessions with ready PRs, and contended runners or PRs that conflict with or supersede each other), which is when it batches through trains. With none active the sibling sessions elect one by a fixed rule (the owner of the P0 PR, else the earliest-created active session); a lone session is its own steward. The holder acknowledges each merge request within a heartbeat window, and a holder that stalls is replaced by re-election without it (owner rulings, 2026-11-07; skill merge-manager-watcher).",
      "sourceKind": "role-registry",
